From: =?UTF-8?q?Ond=C5=99ej=20=C5=A0imon?= <ondrej@dorhawk.software>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:39:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 61/65] win32u: Compare a per-monitor aware rect with the
 monitors' own rects in MonitorFromRect.

A per-monitor aware thread's rects are in each monitor's own pixels. MonitorFromRect compared
them with the monitors' rects at the system DPI, which are the same only while every monitor has
the system DPI. With a 96-DPI display beside a 192-DPI one, a rect on the 96-DPI display matched
no monitor, and a window moved there was judged to be on the other one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index 65ea8612cf..16649ad69e 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -4831,7 +4831,9 @@ static BOOL get_monitor_info( HMONITOR handle, MONITORINFO *info, struct ratio d
 
 static HMONITOR monitor_from_rect( const RECT *rect, UINT flags, struct ratio dpi_from )
 {
-    struct ratio dpi = {system_dpi, 1};
+    /* a per-monitor aware rect is in each monitor's own pixels, which are only the system DPI's
+     * when every monitor has the system DPI: compare it with the monitors' own rects */
+    struct ratio dpi = dpi_from.num ? (struct ratio){system_dpi, 1} : no_dpi;
     struct monitor *monitor;
     HMONITOR ret = 0;
     RECT r;
